WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Install the published package with pipx.
Python and pipx are already installed.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Create a demo login and start remotefs.
Only the isolated demo folder is exposed.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Open the browser interface and sign in.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Open a text file, edit its contents and save.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Create a folder and add it to favourites.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Browse the favourite folder and return.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.500
Download the edited file.
The script verifies the downloaded contents.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:44.460
Now run the same Python service on Linux.
This Mac connects through SSH over Tailscale.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:50.580
Browser on Mac → SSH over Tailscale → Python service on Linux

00:00:50.580 --> 00:01:03.870
Scan the service host’s LAN, with DNS, NetBIOS and IP results

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:16.810
Select 192.168.122.0/24, the NAT VM subnet. No SMB/NFS services
replied during this scan.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:28.310
Map a real SMB server and save credentials

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:33.380
Save a network location to the shortlist

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.360
Browse repository files directly from the NAS

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:42.810
Browse the Python source inside the repository

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:46.080
Shift-click to select a range of files

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:54.540
Right-click a file for actions and download it

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.490
Reload and reopen the saved network location

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:08.280
Map again using saved credentials

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.810
Unmount disconnects the application session; no OS mount was
created

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:22.940
One Python service. No OS mounts. No per-server agent.
NFS uses libnfs; network permissions still apply.
